# Quality Assurance Checklist

**Version**: 1.0  
**Last Updated**: December 30, 2025

---

## ✅ Quality Assurance Checklist

**Before ANY code creation or modification**:

### Code Quality (C# Modernization Standards)

**APPLICABILITY**: 
- **Legacy Code** (`src/legacy/`): Traditional C# style, representative of existing systems
- **Modern Code** (`src/modern/`): Modernized using C# 12–14 features
- **Tests** (`tests/`): Unit tests for both implementations

- [ ] **Parallel Structure Maintained**: Legacy and modern code maintain parallel structure
- [ ] **Functional Equivalence**: Both implementations behave the same
- [ ] **C# Feature Application**: Modern code appropriately demonstrates C# 12–14 features
- [ ] **Code Quality Improved**: Modernization improves readability, safety, or maintainability
- [ ] **Clear Before/After**: Comparison between legacy and modern is clear
- [ ] **Comprehensive Tests**: Tests exist for both implementations
- [ ] **Same Test Cases**: Same test cases applied to both legacy and modern
- [ ] **All Tests Pass**: Both test suites pass successfully
- [ ] **ADR Created**: Architecture Decision Record created for significant decisions
- [ ] **Code Comments**: Clear and helpful comments where needed

### Technical Quality

- [ ] **Build Success**: `dotnet build` completes without errors
- [ ] **Test Success**: `dotnet test` passes for both implementations
- [ ] **Code Style**: Follows C# coding conventions
- [ ] **Meaningful Names**: Variables, methods, and classes have clear names
- [ ] **XML Documentation**: Public APIs have XML documentation comments
- [ ] **No Warnings**: Code compiles without warnings (or warnings are justified)
- [ ] **Character encoding**: UTF-8, no encoding issues

### Documentation Quality

- [ ] **ADR Updated**: Architecture Decision Record created/updated for significant changes
- [ ] **README Updated**: README updated if structure changed
- [ ] **Code Comments**: Code is well-commented where needed
- [ ] **File References**: All file references point to existing files
- [ ] **No Broken Links**: All markdown links resolve correctly

### Modernization Principles

- [ ] **Language-Level Only**: Modernization focuses on language features, not architecture
- [ ] **No Behavioral Changes**: Modernization does not change behavior
- [ ] **Incremental Approach**: Changes are incremental and comparable
- [ ] **Practical Examples**: Examples are realistic and applicable
- [ ] **Benefits Documented**: Benefits of modernization are clear

### Documentation Updates (CRITICAL)

- [ ] ✅ `docs/01_repository-structure.md` updated if structure changed (UPDATE FIRST)
- [ ] ✅ `.github/copilot-instructions.md` updated if structure changed
- [ ] ✅ `README.md` updated if structure changed
- [ ] ✅ `.cursor/rules/02_repository-structure.mdc` updated if structure changed
- [ ] ✅ Related documentation updated

### Pre-Commit Checklist

- [ ] Code builds without errors: `dotnet build`
- [ ] All tests pass: `dotnet test`
- [ ] Both implementations tested: Legacy and modern test suites pass
- [ ] ADR created/updated (if significant change)
- [ ] README updated (if structure changed)
- [ ] No sensitive information included
- [ ] Code follows C# conventions
- [ ] Parallel structure maintained

---

## 🔍 Review Process

### Code Review Checklist

#### Structure Review
- [ ] Legacy and modern code maintain parallel structure
- [ ] Code is organized logically
- [ ] File names are clear and descriptive

#### Modernization Review
- [ ] Modern code demonstrates C# 12–14 features appropriately
- [ ] Before/after comparison is clear
- [ ] Modernization improves code quality

#### Test Review
- [ ] Tests exist for both implementations
- [ ] Same test cases applied to both
- [ ] All tests pass
- [ ] Tests validate correctness

#### Documentation Review
- [ ] ADR created for significant decisions
- [ ] Code comments are clear
- [ ] README updated if needed

---

## 🛠️ Quality Tools

**Use these tools for quality assurance**:

- `dotnet build` - Build verification
- `dotnet test` - Test execution
- Manual code review - Structure and modernization quality
- Markdown linting (for documentation): `npx markdownlint-cli2 "**/*.md"`

---

## 📝 Review Frequency

- **Before committing**: Review all modified files
- **After modernization**: Review both legacy and modern implementations
- **Periodic audits**: Comprehensive review of modernization examples
- **After major changes**: Full review of affected sections

